# SNOBOL4 (scrip-snobol4) program 5, the Rosetta anagrams program of rosetta-snobol4 with a fixed word list in three cells and a recursive reverse REV added: sortw sorts the letters of a word (ARRAY and SORT), countw counts the words of a group, a TABLE groups the words by their sorted letters, a DATA record GROUP carries one group, and the output is the largest group with its key reversed by REV, which recurses once per letter. developer_14 2026-11-22. EXPECTED = skill debugger section 2: a step in at a call enters the routine; a step out stops back in the caller where the call is (the person's reading).
# NOTE on the step out: the breakpoint on line 11 is still set, so a step out from the third level stops at that breakpoint, line 11 of the same frame, before it leaves (a breakpoint stops whatever the step).
{"break": [0, 11]}
{"run": 0}
{"run": 1}
